      "side": 1,
      "message": "Before we get too far into the BackendTexture implementation, I just want to make sure we\u0027re all happy with their API and what we want to support in regards to them. I\u0027ve add a few comments/question to start the discussion, but would love to hear others opinions.",
      "revId": "0d1d440444d8b479b94b799f56c7efe44c9e00bf",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b656072_5e1afeaa",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/include/BackendTexture.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 25,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-29T15:28:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should BackendTexture we taking a ref to the Mtl Textures? For Vulkan and D3D (and Ganesh GL) the BackendTexture does not hold a ref of the backend object. Instead these are all treated as raw handles and the client is required to keep the backend object alive as long as the BackendTexture is wrapped in a Skia object. So we could match that same system in Metal by only taking a mtl::Handle instead (i.e. id\u003cMTLTexture\u003e). This would allow the client to think of all backends the same.\n\nIf we do this, the question becomes what do we do internally in mtl::Texture. Right now that class holds an sk_cfp\u003cid\u003cMTLTexture\u003e\u003e. It is a little weird for us to internally take a ref to the texture when publicly we\u0027re telling the client they have to keep the object alive. Maybe its not weird for metal to be taking a ref to the object since the metal api itself is a ref counted API so we should stick to that model.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 25,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 25,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "0d1d440444d8b479b94b799f56c7efe44c9e00bf",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "06c5afbe_78a26482",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/BackendTexture.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 49,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-29T15:28:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This awkwardness all comes from the fact that we store an sk_cfp of the mtl texture. If we didn\u0027t have the BackendTexture take a ref then this assignment would be trivial.\n\nAn alternative here is that we have BackendTexture take an mtl::Handle (id\u003cMTLTexture), but state that BackendTexture will call Retain and Release on the object. Then inside here we can be explicit with when we need to Release the previous texture and not have the ugliness of calling fMtlTexture.release() on an uninitialized sk_cfp object.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 44,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 49,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "0d1d440444d8b479b94b799f56c7efe44c9e00bf",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eb606fa5_0595afca",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/mtl/MtlGpu.mm",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 93,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-29T15:33:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh another question, Should calling context-\u003edestroyBackendTexture(backendTexture), clear out the backendTexture (i.e. set it to be invalid) or just leave everything as is? Currently Ganesh just leaves it as is since the dtor on most backends doesn\u0027t do anything anyways. But with Metal this means the MTLTexture doesn\u0027t get destroyed until the ~BackendTexture. We could unref the texture here instead.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 93,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "0d1d440444d8b479b94b799f56c7efe44c9e00bf",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "31896a3d_4478ee91",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/mtl/MtlTexture.mm",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-29T15:28:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What do we think the \"caps\" requirements should be for making a BackendTexture. Do we restrict things to the same requirements that Skia has? For example, for Skia isTexturable currently requires the format to also be linearly filterable when sampled in the shader. Or what if the client asks to add the MTLTextureUsageRenderTarget flag to a format that Skia itself doesn\u0027t render (e.g. 101010102 because Skia can\u0027t handle the 2 alpha correctly when rendering)? Should we block the client from making these BackendTexture objects or be more open to making them as long as the conform the APIs specs?\n\nIf we\u0027re more open about making them we can still restrict and reject them when a client goes to wrap the BackendTexture into Skia.\n\nThough on the flip side do we really see clients who want Skia to make the textures for them but don\u0027t intend to immediately wrap them back into Skia? Assuming that doesn\u0027t happen maybe it makes sense to just be restrictive on BackendTexture creation from the get go.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 30,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "0d1d440444d8b479b94b799f56c7efe44c9e00bf",
